{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-40-1","title":"Job 40:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Job humbles himself to God. 6 God stirs him up to shew his righteousness, power, and wisdom. 16 Of the behemoth.</p>\n<p>6; 38:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-2","title":"Job 40:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Shall. 9:3; 33:13; Ec 6:10; Isa 45:9-11; 50:8; 1Co 10:22 instruct. Isa 40:14; 1Co 2:16 he that reproveth. 3:11,12,20,23; 7:12,19-21; 9:17,18,32-35; 10:3-7,14-17; 13:21-27 14:16,17; 16:11-21; 19:6-11; 27:2; 30:21; Eze 18:2; Mt 20:11 Ro 9:19-23; 11:34-36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-4","title":"Job 40:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Behold. 42:6; Ge 18:27; 32:10; 2Sa 24:10; 1Ki 19:4; Ezr 9:6,15; Ne 9:33 Ps 51:4,5; Isa 6:5; 53:6; 64:6; Da 9:5,7; Lu 5:8; 15:18,19; 18:13 1Ti 1:15 what. 9:31-35; 16:21; 23:4-7; 31:37 I will. 21:5; 29:9; Jud 18:19; Ps 39:9; Pr 30:32; Mic 7:16; Hab 2:20 Zec 2:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-5","title":"Job 40:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>but I will not. 34:31,32; Ro 3:19 twice. 33:14; 2Ki 6:10; Ps 62:11 but I will proceed. Jer 31:18,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-6","title":"Job 40:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>out. 38:1; Ps 50:3,4; Heb 12:18-20; 2Pe 3:10-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-7","title":"Job 40:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Gird. 13:22; 23:3,4; 38:3 I. 42:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-8","title":"Job 40:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Wilt. Ps 51:4; Ro 3:4 disannul. Isa 14:27; 28:18; Ga 3:15,17; Heb 7:18 wilt thou condemn. 10:3; 27:2-6; 32:2; 34:5,6; 35:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-9","title":"Job 40:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Hast. 9:4; 23:6; 33:12,13; Ex 15:6; Ps 89:10,13; Isa 45:9; 1Co 10:22 canst. 37:4,5; Ps 39:3-9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-10","title":"Job 40:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Deck. 39:19; Ps 93:1; 104:1,2; Isa 59:17 majesty. 1Ch 29:11; Ps 21:5; 45:3,4; Mt 6:13; 2Pe 1:16,17; Jude 1:24,25 glory. Ex 28:2; Ps 50:2; 90:16,17; 149:4; Isa 4:2; *marg: 1Co 15:54</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-11","title":"Job 40:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Cast. 20:23; 27:22; De 32:22; Ps 78:49,50; 144:6; Ro 2:8,9 behold. Ex 9:16,17; 15:6; 18:11; Isa 2:11,12,17; 10:12-19; Eze 28:2 Da 4:37; 5:20-23; Ob 1:3,4; Mal 4:1; Lu 18:14; Ac 12:22,23; Jas 4:6 1Pe 5:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-12","title":"Job 40:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>tread. Ps 60:12; Pr 15:25; Isa 10:6; Zec 10:5; Mal 4:3; Ro 16:20 in. 36:20; Ec 11:3; Ac 1:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-13","title":"Job 40:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Hide. 14:13; Ps 49:14; Isa 2:10 bind. 36:13; Es 7:8; Joh 11:44</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-14","title":"Job 40:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>that. Ps 44:3,6; Isa 40:29; Ro 5:6; Eph 2:4-9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-15","title":"Job 40:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>behemoth.[Beh�m�wth ,] Perhaps an extinct dinosaur, maybe a Diplodocus or Brachiosaurus, the exact meaning is unknown. Some translate as elephant or hippopotamus but from the description in Job 40:15-24 , this is patently absurd.</p>\n<p>which. Ge 1:24-26 he. 20; 39:8; Ps 104:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-17","title":"Job 40:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>moveth. or, setteth up. the. 41:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-18","title":"Job 40:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>7:12; Isa 48:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-19","title":"Job 40:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>the chief. 26:13; Ps 104:24 he that. Ps 7:12; Isa 27:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-20","title":"Job 40:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>the mountains. 15; Ps 147:8,9 where. Ps 104:14,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-21","title":"Job 40:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>the reed. Isa 19:6,7; 35:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-22","title":"Job 40:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>the willows. Le 23:40; Isa 15:7; Eze 17:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-23","title":"Job 40:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>drinketh. Heb. oppresseth. Isa 37:25 hasteth. Ps 55:8; Isa 28:16 Jordan. Ge 13:10; Jos 3:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-40-24","title":"Job 40:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":40,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":40,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>Or, Will any take him in his sight, or bore his nose with agin?</p>\n<p>41:1,2</p>"}]}